### 錦2 | _(2)Kam_ [[gam2]]

$$
R
  ⾦ + 8
  ⼱ + 13
U
  U+9326
A
  ==
  - {𡄎=⿰口錦} (for Cantonese particle of partiality)
  - 锦 (Mainland simplified)
  ==
F
  ==
  - (F2.37 錦) 五色絲所織
  ==
W
  ====
  - [[Page~125 #3: (2)錦]]
    ==
    - ~~A kind~~ ``Ornamental work`` of variegated silk ~~used in ornamental work~~ [[Kangxi: 襄色織文也 etc.]];
    - embroidered, worked, or knit in colors;
    - elegant, figurative fine writing;
    - flowery, pictured;
    - _~~(1)(i/)~~ ``(i/)(3)`` (2)kam_
        [[ji3 gam2 衣錦]],
        the gentry, official persons;
    - _(2)kam (4)ch(')au_
        [[gam2 cau4 錦綢]],
        figured pongee;
    - _shap(9) (2)kam (2)(u/)n t(i/)p(9)_
        [[sap6 gam2 wun2 dip6 什錦碗碟]]
        colored chinaware;
    - _(2)kam sau(3) (4)man_
        [[gam2 sau3 man4 錦繡文]],
        an elegant style.
    ==
  ====
C
  ==
  - Williams' "A kind of variegated silk used in ornamental work":
    This is a poor rendering of both Kangxi 襄色織文也,
    which defines 錦 as the ornamental work (not the silk),
    and Fan Wan 五色絲所織,
    which defines 錦 as 所織 "that weaved" (not the silk).
  - Williams' 衣錦: Corrected _(1)(i/)_ (ji1) to _(i/)(3)_ (ji3).
  ==
L
  ====
  * 【錦】 (kimX)
    ==
    - (_noun-like_) brocade
    ==
  ====
E
  ====
  - 【錦】 (gam2)
    ++
    1. A particle of partial amount.
       ==
       - 食錦啲先 (sik6 gam2 di1 sin1): "Eat [a] bit of [it] first."
       - 冇錦唿 (mou5 gam2 fat1): "Lost [a] patch of [it]."
       ==
    ++
  ====
  --
  The spelling 錦 is arbitrary.
  The alternative spelling {𡄎=⿰口錦} has poorer font support.
  --
  --
  The spellings 噉 and 咁 are inadvisable,
  because [噉~gam2 ("like so")](#cantonese-噉) is a distinct word.
  Unlike 噉~gam2 ("like so"), the particle 錦~gam2
  *cannot* be pronounced [kom].
  --
$$

